The shape assumptions differ at the attention–MoE boundary: single-device GDN uses `[B,T,H]`, while routed experts read axis 2 as the token count in `[1,1,S,H]`. I’m checking full attention separately because its head-concatenation operation may change the rank before MoE receives it.
