The cache audit found two distinct failures: bound-cache prefill can silently use a private concat cache when `chunk_page_table` is absent, and paged fill writes at page-relative offset zero even when attention reads at a nonzero `chunk_start_idx`. The lowered code also confirms batch limits in GDN state and full-attention decode. I’ll separate these definite contract failures from precision risks that still need hardware measurements.
