     1	# AutoDebug: initial Qwen3.5-35B-A3B functional decoder
     2	
     3	Investigation date: 2026-10-10 UTC. Inspection only: no TT device access, target execution, source edits, launcher invocation, or additional agents. This report is the only file written by this investigation.
     4	
     5	## Findings at a glance
     6	
     7	The adapter does not yet implement the requested functional contract. There are several independent problems; removing the reported FIR host upload alone will not make the decoder correct.
     8	
     9	| Priority | Finding | Scope and confidence |
    10	|---|---|---|
    11	| 1 | Every GDN prefill constructs and uploads a Torch FIR selector, including aligned lengths. Padded scans construct another host mask. | Direct call-chain proof; violates device-only forward and prevents capture of that prefill path. |
    12	| 1 | Rank-3 single-device layer activations reach rank-4 MoE code without conversion. Hidden width 2048 is interpreted as the token/batch count. | Both layer kinds, prefill and decode; direct incompatible shape calculations. |
    13	| 1 | Default GDN chunk preprocessing uses diagonal regularization `alpha=0.25`, changing the reference recurrence. | GDN prefill with default environment, including aligned inputs. Mathematical discrepancy, independent of quantization. |
    14	| 1 | Paged-cache binding does not ensure paged prefill. Fill offsets, logical lengths, and request rows are not fully represented by the adapter. | Full attention: missing chunk table, non-page-aligned continuation, partial pages, and nonzero request slots. |
    15	| 1 | Batch support is contradicted by fixed B=1 GDN state and the full-attention paged decode axis conversion. | B>1; independently broken even after repairing MoE rank. |
    16	| 2 | The boundary rejects unpadded lengths, returns physical-length outputs, and does not bound whole-call GDN work. | Arbitrary lengths and native 262144-token context are not implemented by the initial wrapper. |
    17	| 2 | Reuse silently selects BFP4/BFP8 weights, BF16 persistent GDN state, and LoFi projections. | Confirmed policy mismatch with an evidence-backed functional baseline; no measured PCC failure is asserted. |
    18	
    19	Runtime manifestation remains unmeasured. No supplied runtime trace establishes which error happens first on hardware. In particular, attention/state work runs before the malformed MoE call; the MoE failure can hide earlier numerical or cache defects and leave already-advanced state behind.
    20	
