# Qwen3.5-35B-A3B functional decoder — in progress

Target: `Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B`, revision
`59d61f3ce65a6d9863b86d2e96597125219dc754`. Checkout base:
`98dc4ae62ccfc32836ddcfad50f9fd97863612d4`, branch
`feat/qwen3-5-35b-a3b`. One Blackhole ASIC, mesh 1×1. Four ASICs are available.
This stage does not implement a full model or serving adapter.

The current implementation is being validated. No stage pass, physical context
reduction, performance result, or independent review pass is claimed.

## Interface

`FunctionalDecoder.from_state_dict(state_dict, *, hf_config, layer_idx,
mesh_device, tensor_cache_path=None, max_batch_size=32)` loads the real checkpoint
keys through the Qwen36 weight loader. The layer uses real target dimensions:
hidden 2048; full attention Q16/KV2/head256; linear attention key16/value32/head128;
256 routed experts, top8, intermediate512 and gated shared expert512.

`prefill_forward(hidden_states, *, start_pos=0, page_table=None,
request_slots=None, valid_len=None)` accepts logical `[B,T,2048]` TTNN tensors.
It retains state for explicit prefix continuation and returns all logical rows.
Bounded aligned chunks use the existing attention/GDN and sparse MoE kernels;
unaligned tails use device-only single-token computation to avoid padding state
updates. Full attention uses absolute positions and caller-owned paged KV.

`decode_forward(hidden_states, *, position_tensor=None, page_table=None,
request_slots=None)` consumes `[B,1,2048]` device activations. Full attention reads
absolute current positions from a device tensor and looks up partial RoPE on
device. Linear attention uses persistent recurrent/convolution state per slot.
Batch rows execute separately on the single ASIC and preserve independent state.
`bind_paged_kv_cache(key_cache, value_cache)` binds external BF16 paged caches.
`reset_request_state(request_slots=None)` resets fresh recurrent requests outside
trace capture; callers must not reset explicit continuations.

## Evidence so far

Initial real-weight 128-token smoke PCC (superseded code; diagnostic baseline):

| Kind | Prefill | Eager decode | Artifact |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| full_attention | 0.998625 | 0.998601 | `full_smoke.json` |
| linear_attention | 0.996777 | 0.998699 | `linear_smoke.json` |

129-token checks on the chunk/tail path, including repeated traced decode with
`TT_METAL_TRACE_ALLOC_TRACKING=1 TT_METAL_TRACE_ALLOC_SKIP_PROGRAM_CACHE=0`:

| Kind | Prefill | Traced decode | Identical replay | Artifact |
|---|---:|---:|---|---|
| full_attention | 0.998626 | 0.997459 | yes | `full_trace129.json` |
| linear_attention | 0.996777 | 0.998731 | yes | `linear_trace129.json` |

Acceptance remains PCC ≥0.995. These small tests do not establish long-context
capability, batch coverage, complete trace reuse, watcher cleanliness, or warmed
performance. See `work_log.md` and `../context_contract.json` for remaining gates.

## Trace output lifetime

The harness allocates weights, inputs, KV, recurrent state, and reset snapshots
before capture. Program-cache misses are forbidden during capture. Only the
specific final trace output is acknowledged to the allocation tracker; it is
read before replay overwrites it. No whole-forward allocation exemption is used.

## Reproduction

From the tt-metal checkout, source `../scripts/environment.sh`, then run:

```bash
TT_METAL_TRACE_ALLOC_TRACKING=1 TT_METAL_TRACE_ALLOC_SKIP_PROGRAM_CACHE=0 \
python -u -m models.autoports.qwen_qwen3_5_35b_a3b.tests.run_layer \
  --layer 0 --length 129 --trace \
  --output models/autoports/qwen_qwen3_5_35b_a3b/doc/functional_decoder/linear_trace129.json
```

Use `--layer 3` for full attention. Hardware jobs must run serially.
